    "repo": "swesmith/msiemens__tinydb.10644a0e",
    "problem_statement": "CachingMiddleware returns stale data after cache is populated\n\n#### Description\n\nThe CachingMiddleware is not properly returning cached data. After writing data to storage, subsequent reads return the data from storage instead of the cached version, which defeats the purpose of caching and can lead to performance issues.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb.middlewares import CachingMiddleware\nfrom tinydb.storages import MemoryStorage\n\n# Create a caching middleware with memory storage\nstorage = CachingMiddleware(MemoryStorage)\nstorage()\n\n# Write some data\ndoc = {'name': 'John', 'age': 30}\nstorage.write(doc)\n\n# Read the data - this should return the cached version\nresult = storage.read()\nprint(\"Expected:\", doc)\nprint(\"Actual:\", result)\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when the cache is populated (not None) - instead of returning the cached data, it incorrectly reads from the underlying storage again."
  },
